# Multi-level tenant host parsing (P1 EPIC E)

## SoT

Parser lives in **`@app-tour/tenant-kernel`**: `parseMultiLevelTenantHost`, `isPlatformAdminHost`.

| Host pattern | Outcome | Surface |
|--------------|---------|---------|
| `admin.{root}` | `platform_admin` | Platform Control Center |
| `{club}.admin.{root}` | `club_admin` | Club operator panel |
| `{club}.portal.{root}` | `club_portal` | Public registration portal |
| `{club}.{root}` | `club_apex` | Marketing / club apex |

Single-level `{label}.{root}` behavior is unchanged for valid tenant labels (`parseWorkspaceTenantLabelFromHost` fallback).

`admin` remains in `DEFAULT_TENANT_HOST_RESERVED_LABELS` for **club apex** labels — platform admin is detected **before** reserved-label checks (DEC-P1-021).

## Web wiring

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `apps/web/src/tenant/resolve-multi-level-host.ts` | Env root wrapper around kernel parser |
| `apps/web/src/platform/is-platform-admin-host.ts` | Re-exports kernel `isPlatformAdminHost` |
| `apps/web/src/tenant/resolve-host-tenant.ts` | Dev map for `*.admin.localhost`, `*.portal.localhost`, apex |
| `apps/web/src/tenant/session-host-binding.ts` | Session tenant bind for club admin + legacy apex |
| `apps/web/middleware.ts` | Platform vs operator isolation |

### Middleware isolation

| Host | `/platform/*` | Operator `/dashboard` etc. |
|------|---------------|----------------------------|
| `admin.{root}` | allowed (platform session) | redirect → `/platform` |
| `{club}.admin.{root}` | **404** | allowed (operator session) |
| `{club}.{root}` apex | forward (no operator gate on public paths) | **blocked** on protected admin paths |
| `{club}.portal.{root}` | forward | **blocked** on protected admin paths |

## Marketing / portal

Dev host maps use kernel parser:

- Marketing: `club_apex` → `resolveTenantIdFromDevHost`
- Portal: `club_portal` → `resolveTenantIdFromDevHost`

## API

`apps/api/src/middleware/resolve-tenant-from-host.ts` — extracts club subdomain from `Host` for ingress alignment (JWT remains auth SoT in production).

Public guest routes **`GET /public/tenant-branding`** and **`GET /public/tenant-context`** call `resolveTenantSubdomainFromHostHeader` (not single-level `parseWorkspaceTenantLabelFromHost` alone) so `{club}.admin.{root}` and `{club}.portal.{root}` resolve to the same subdomain registry row as club apex. Without this, web BFF operator login on club admin hosts falls back to `TOUR_OPS_DEV_TENANT_ID` and pending owner invites fail OTP authorization.

### Session bind vs BFF tenant resolution (P1 EPIC H)

Operator BFF login (`resolveOperatorBffTenantId`) resolves tenant in order: static dev map → **`GET /public/tenant-context`** → `TOUR_OPS_DEV_TENANT_ID` fallback.

Root layout bootstrap (`resolveBootstrapAppSessionForHostAsync`) uses the same **static map → tenant-context** order before env fallback so `AppSession` (`tenantId`, `pluginId`, workspace draft keys) matches the operator JWT on freshly provisioned `{club}.admin.{root}` hosts. When an operator `session` cookie is present, layout re-binds bootstrap from JWT claims (`tenant_id`, `workspace_id`, role) while preserving registry-resolved `pluginId`.

Owner handoff E2E: invite accept must be followed by a **fresh OTP login** so the session JWT carries membership `workspace_id` (not the pre-accept pending-invite dev fallback).

Middleware session bind (`resolveExpectedTenantIdForHost`) must **not** apply the env fallback on **unmapped multi-level club hosts** (`club_admin`, `club_portal`, `club_apex`). Those hosts are provisioned dynamically (platform create-club); only the registry knows `{subdomain} → tenantId`.

| Host | Static map | Session bind expected tenant |
|------|------------|------------------------------|
| `denali.admin.localhost` | smoke UUID | strict match |
| `handoff-abc.admin.localhost` (new club) | none | **null** (fail-open) |
| `operator.localhost` (legacy apex) | smoke UUID | strict match |
| unmapped legacy apex | none | `TOUR_OPS_DEV_TENANT_ID` |

When expected tenant is **null**, `sessionTenantMatchesHost` fail-opens (session JWT tenant is trusted). This prevents `AUTH_TENANT_HOST_MISMATCH` on invite accept after OTP login on a freshly provisioned club admin host while keeping strict bind for known smoke subdomains.

## Verify (EPIC E gate)

```bash
pnpm --filter @app-tour/tenant-kernel test
cd apps/web && NODE_ENV=test node --import tsx --import ./test/register-dom.mjs --test --test-force-exit \
  test/multi-level-host-parse.spec.ts \
  test/resolve-multi-level-host.spec.ts \
  test/session-host-binding-multilevel.spec.ts \
  test/platform-host-isolation.spec.ts \
  test/platform-middleware-imports.spec.ts
```

Note: `multi-level-host-parse.spec.ts` lives under `packages/tenant-kernel/test/`; web specs import `@app-tour/tenant-kernel` after `pnpm --filter @app-tour/tenant-kernel run build`.
